title: Debug Menu
sidebar:
  order: 2
---

The debug menu lets you warp to maps, trigger battles, edit inventory and stats, and more — without playing through the game normally.

## Enabling the debug menu

The debug menu is enabled by default. If it's been disabled, set `DX_DEBUG_MENU` to `1` in `dx/config.h`:

```c
#define DX_DEBUG_MENU 1
```

## Controls

Once in-game, press **D-Pad Left** to open the debug menu.

| Button | Action |
|--------|--------|
| D-Pad | Select option |
| R | Confirm selection |
| L | Cancel / close menu |

## Features

The debug menu has many options. Here are some highlights:

- **Load Map** — warp to any map by name
- **Load Battle** — start any battle formation directly
- **Story Progress** — change the current story progress value
- **Inventory** — add or remove items, badges, and key items
- **Stats** — edit HP, FP, BP, star points, coins, star pieces, and level
- **Partners** — add partners and change the active partner

## Sound Player

Open **Sound Player**, then choose **Sound** for the hexadecimal sound-effect
Play/Stop controls or **Music** for a named song browser.

In Music, Up/Down selects a song and wraps at the ends. Left/Right moves nine
entries at a time and stops at the ends. Press **R** to play or restart, **Z** to
stop, and **L** to go back. Returning to the browser retains the selected entry.
Pressing **R** again also replays a finished jingle without needing to stop first.

The list is generated from the project's resolved song IDs, so it follows song
additions and deletions. An unmodified DX build lists the 143 named vanilla
songs. Selecting a song does not change audio assets or save data; normal map
and battle music scripts can take over playback.

## Quick launch

To skip the title screen and load a save file immediately, set `DX_QUICK_LAUNCH` in `dx/config.h`:

```c
#define DX_QUICK_LAUNCH 1
```

You can also quick-launch directly into a specific battle. Uncomment and edit this line in `config.h`:

```c
#define DX_QUICK_LAUNCH_BATTLE "nok:goomba_2", "nok_01"
```

## Performance profiler

Set `USE_PROFILER` to `1` in `dx/config.h` to show a performance profiler overlay. Toggle it in-game with **L + D-Pad Up**.
